WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.890
Deep in a flooded mine, the
water lies in total darkness.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.200
No sunlight ever reaches it.

3
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.480
Yet bacteria grow there.

4
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:14.270
There is no food at all: just
dissolved iron and a few gases.

5
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.520
Like every cell, each
needs carbon compounds:

6
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:21.460
sugars, proteins, lipids, nucleic acids.

7
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.730
So how can anything grow
down there, in the dark,

8
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.680
with nothing to eat?

9
00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:30.430
In this mission, you'll sort
living things into two camps:

10
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.890
those that make their
own carbon compounds,

11
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.180
and those that take them from others.

12
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.050
Then you'll follow a meal
through a heterotroph:

13
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.430
digested, absorbed, then
built into its own molecules.

14
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.980
Your mission: find out how bacteria
can grow in total darkness,

15
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.430
with no food at all.
